Vela's new tab is the profile's `pyxis.newtab.url` pref when set (added
2026-11-16). Firefox removed its new-tab pref in 41; the remaining override is
AboutNewTab.newTabURL, which only extensions set, and the browser profile runs
with extensions off. Nova writes the pref (and browser.startup.homepage) into
the browser window's profile only, pointing at the start page the browser app
ships (pyxis-experience packages/apps/browser/public/start/). An unset pref
leaves Firefox's own about:newtab. browser.js's isInitialPage compares against
the same URL, so the address bar stays empty on it.

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
The unified diff below is generated from the checkout and is applied with
  git apply gecko/patches/pyxis/<path>.PYXIS_DIFF
(or `patch -p1 <`). Everything above this line is rationale, not content;
git apply ignores it. Regenerate with scripts/regen-gecko-patches.sh.
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

diff --git a/browser/modules/AboutNewTab.sys.mjs b/browser/modules/AboutNewTab.sys.mjs
index d35c0c0b3fa9..1a27881487f9 100644
--- a/browser/modules/AboutNewTab.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/modules/AboutNewTab.sys.mjs
@@ -76,6 +76,15 @@ export const AboutNewTab = {
 
     // More initialization happens here
     this.toggleActivityStream(true);
+
+    // PYXIS: Vela's new tab is the profile's `pyxis.newtab.url` when set (Nova
+    // writes it for the browser window: Vela's own start page). Firefox has
+    // no pref for this since 41; the override setter is what extensions use,
+    // and the browser profile runs with extensions off.
+    const pyxisNewTab = Services.prefs.getStringPref("pyxis.newtab.url", "");
+    if (pyxisNewTab) {
+      this.newTabURL = pyxisNewTab;
+    }
     this.initialized = true;
 
     Services.obs.addObserver(this, BROWSER_READY_NOTIFICATION);
